<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids remain weak.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids remain weak.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat cash bids remained weaker on Friday as many producers continued to wait for better prices, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is very quiet. There are not very many receipts. Farmers are still hanging on,&quot; a Minnesota dealer said. &quot;We have to get competitive in the world market and we are not.&quot;</p>
<p>December MGE spring wheat futures lost five cents to end at $4.29-1/4 a bushel.</p>
<p>Dealers noted that since much of the harvest is over, activity is expected to be slow for about a month.</p>
<p>Movement is slow, one said. But another dealer said the lack of exports was the reason for the slack activity.  </p>
